The attached image (Figure 4) demonstrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are actively transported to the draining lymph nodes and target specific antigen-presenting cells. Plot A shows the detection and phenotyping of Nano-11-containing myeloid cells, with an increase in these cells from Day 1 to Day 2, then a decrease by Day 7. Plot B quantifies this trend, illustrating the percentage of Nano-11+ myeloid cells peaking at Day 2. Plot C reveals that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) consistently contain the highest proportion of Nano-11+ cells (60-80%) across all time points. Plot D indicates that MigDCs also have the highest mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) per cell, suggesting they take up more Nano-11 than other APC subtypes, enhancing antigen delivery to these key immunopotentiating cells.